    "sentence_translations": [
      "Fresh Fried Rice",
      "",
      "There was a person called Little Hei.",
      "One day Little Hei was hungry, and went to eat again at a restaurant that he went to often.",
      "But he didn’t recognize the waiter, so he asked the waiter, “You’re a new restaurant, right?”",
      "The waiter answered: “Yes, this is the new menu.”",
      "",
      "Little Hei said, “Your food is very expensive!”",
      "",
      "The waiter said, “It’s because this restaurant is very expensive! What do you want to eat?”",
      "",
      "Little Hei said: “Why is your fresh fried rice this expensive? Because it’s very fresh? It must be very tasty!”",
      "",
      "The waiter said, “It’s very fresh all right, but I don’t know if it’s tasty or not.”",
      "",
      "Little Hei ordered a portion of fresh fried rice, but he thought that the fried rice was very unpalatable.",
      "So he asked the person who cooked the food to come and see him.",
      "",
      "Little Hei asked, “Excuse me, is your rice from last week? It tastes very bad! Why is it called fresh fried rice?”",
      "",
      "The person who cooked it said, “Hello! It’s because I’m called Xin Xian.”"
    ]
  }
